While this game, I'd say, is a bit behind TSE in terms of quality, I deem TFE to be a very good game nevertheless :
-the gunplay is rather solid;
-very fun 16 player Co-Op;
-the level design, while simplistic, often gives opportunities to look for resources and secrets and often isn't too restrictive;
-I find the esthetic to be quite nice and the music wonderfully fitting the game;
-the enemy variety is very adequate;
-and, the most importantly, I find the whole gameplay to be captivating. Serious Sam has a lot to do with knowing how to react to the different enemies, their movement, their attacks. And because of the large enemy variety, one not only has to decide what enemy is the most dangerous at that given time and which weapon suits that particular situation the most, but one also has to move in such precise ways so that he escaped all those different projectiles and melee attacks, at the same time being aware of his surroundings - this could be called 'Dancing with the enemies' : constantly and precisely moving, jumping and shooting amidst enemies, rockets and whatever the game throws at you. It requires skill, decision making and just general knowledge of the game- so Serious Sam is not a mindless shooter, contrary to the popular belief.

